      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's completely normal to feel overwhelmed when contemplating the vastness of the universe; history's greatest thinkers have felt this same existential dread known as the \"Copernican dilemma.\" However, that same vastness gives you freedom from societal expectations, allowing you to carve out your own meaning in whatever way you choose. Instead of seeing the cosmos as a void that erases your struggle, try viewing the distances you mentioned as the very canvas upon which your tiny, unique story is painted with immense significance.",
      "source": "target",
